I think I have found another problem with the Mac version of Nethack 3.0.7:

My barbarian character just died on level 27, so I decided to reboot up
a copy of him so that I could try out level 28 (with the castle and all).  I
was in the exporer mode.  After lowering the drawbridge, I found the first
room with all of the soldgers in it, and, being that I've never been here
before, went '/' to identify them.  It told me what they were, and asked
if I wanted more infomation, I pressed 'y'.  I read the extra stuff of these
creatures, and instead of moving the mouse over the press 'Quit', I just
pressed <return>.  The 'More' button highlighted, and things went wierd.
It started scrolling as fast as it could through what looked like part of
the binary code (much like when I do it on the Unix machine here on campus).
I looks like something went astray, and the pointer (or whatever) got into
the binary code, started to print it, and never knew when to stop.  I had
to restart the machine to regain control.

This happened last Friday, and sence then, I haven't seen another soldier to
see if this happens again.

Otherwise, I've been having a lot of fun with it.  Thanks.

